// Title: ESXi Admin Permission Assigned To Account Via ESXCLI
// Sigma ID: 9691f58d-92c1-4416-8bf3-2edd753ec9cf
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-09-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, execution, privilege-escalation, T1059.012, T1098
// Description: Detects execution of the "esxcli" command with the "system" and "permission" flags in order to
//   assign admin permissions to an account.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/esxcli-command-reference/7.0.0/namespace/esxcli_system.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_esxcli_permission_change_admin.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/esxcli" and ProcessCommandLine contains "system" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " permission " and ProcessCommandLine contains " set" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Admin")
